  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1237 PM CDT Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nAs we continue into the first week of November, present model\nagreement does want to give us a little break from activity with a\nridge building in behind the system Monday. This should allow for\na bit of a drier day for Tuesday with chance of precipitation\nbelow 10 percent that afternoon. However, conditions will stay\ncool for the day with afternoon highs in the upper 50s to 60s for\nthe day. Moving into Wednesday and rest of the work week does look\nto keep this break brief as models try to force a series of\ntroughs and associated upper-level lows across the Panhandles.\nHowever, present deterministic model runs are still trying get the\ntiming of these troughs with current GFS running much faster on\nthese systems then the ECMWF. For now, present ensembles are\nfavoring Wednesday for the first of these systems with chances of\nprecipitation most across the Northern Panhandles at around 10 to\n30 percent. After which, they call for the secondary system\nsometime over next weekend with present runs favoring more\nwidespread chances. Otherwise, look for temperatures to stay on\nthe cooler side, with afternoon highs in the 60s to low 70s.",
